# Local dashboard contracts

Use AGENTS.md and the active Phase 26 plan with
`archive/implementation-history/plans/phase-26-dashboard-contract.md`.
Codex owns this rule and the plans; implementation does not edit governance.

- Phase 26 explicitly introduces a loopback HTTP adapter and dashboard CLI;
  historical Phase 21's no-HTTP scope does not forbid this later approved work.
- `ai_dev_loop` owns SQLite/artifact reads. Share semantic application queries
  with JSON Integration API; domain rules import no web/database frameworks.
- Read only with validated scheduler state/lineage and confined registered
  artifact readers; no migration, repair, tick, reservation, Git or model turn.
- Start cohort includes Cursor/Codex implementer and Codex reviewer execution
  effects. Reviewer rounds include review effects only; codex_implementer is never
  a reviewer. Preserve historical provider defaults and current role/retry fields.
  Cursor SDK initial/correction inference keeps the stable `cursor.run_turn`
  execution meaning. Exclude CLI chat/SDK agent creation,
  preflight/probes, ingestion and unknown effects. Project comes from projectName.
- Distinguish started cohort from submissions/review rounds/process seconds.
  Retry grouping is runId+iteration; recorded parallel process seconds are summed.
  Missing historic evidence is explicit; partial pages never become global totals.
- Inputs/results/time budgets are bounded by the shared contract. Use typed
  additive DTOs, explicit capability and major compatibility. Summary output
  excludes bodies, sessions, private paths, environments and credentials.
- HTTP binds 127.0.0.1 only, uses fixed same-origin typed read routes and package
  assets; no login, remote control, arbitrary paths/commands, wildcard CORS or CDN.
- Keep UI source strings escaped. Content loads explicitly by exact resource ID,
  stays memory-only, is paginated and cleared on close/reselection/filter change.
  Do not reconstruct exact implementer prompts or infer review-attempt linkage;
  reviewer-content never targets a Codex implementer attempt.
- UI components depend on DashboardDataSource, not localhost or future Hub URLs.
  Live polling obeys visibility/Pause/cancellation/generations and bounded work;
  sensitive readers never auto-refresh. No durable dashboard cache or telemetry.
- Node is build/test-only; shipped Python wheel includes required static assets.
  Use isolated temporary resources/fake providers for acceptance. Scheduler driver,
  timer, root YAML, reviewer contracts and real workstation installation stay out
  of implementation scope; final operator walkthrough is separate acceptance.
